Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:12:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Add the thermal
 sensors on the Surface Laptop 7

The Surface Laptop 7's SAM reports nine temperature sensors (TMP
available-sensors mask 0x0f1f, instances 1-5 and 9-12). They answer
surface_temp's requests: every instance returns a temperature and a
name ("I_RTS1" to "I_RTS5" and "I_RTS1" to "I_RTS4", the name
response's second byte telling the two banks apart). The group left
them out with a TODO from before surface_temp existed.

Add the TMP sensor device to the Surface Laptop 7 group, so
surface_temp binds and the sensors show up as the surface_thermal
hwmon device.

Instance 4 reads 0 (0 K) on the 13.8"; the others read 32-42 C at
idle.
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index 311f02a1a..ad3320516 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -317,3 +317,3 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sl7[] = {
 	&ssam_node_hid_sam_keyboard,
-	/* TODO: evaluate thermal sensors devices when we get a driver for that */
+	&ssam_node_tmp_sensors,
 	NULL,
-- 
2.56.1

